# ONT k-selection sweep (td-4e19d.28) — artifact policy.
#
# COMMITTED (the durable knowledge tier): ont_k_sweep_results.tsv,
# ont_k_sweep_summary.tsv, verdict_stats.tsv, README.md. These are small,
# plain-text, and are the deliverable the pre-registration decision rests on.
# (verdict_stats.tsv was omitted from this list until td-4blm; it has been
# tracked all along, and this file documents the tracked/untracked split that
# the shrink guard's whole argument rests on, so the omission mattered.)
#
# IGNORED (bulky and deterministically regenerable from the committed script
# plus its recorded seeds): the downloaded reference, per-cell simulated reads,
# per-cell contig FASTAs, per-cell QUAST output trees, and the per-cell JSON
# resume checkpoints. Re-running `benchmarking/ont_k_sweep.jl` with the same
# --output-dir reconstructs all of it.
#
# NOTE the per-cell contig FASTAs are large in the low-k regime specifically
# (ONT/30x/k=11 emits ~149k contigs), which is exactly why they are not tracked.
cells/
refs/
shard-logs/
